Dine in  |  Brunch  |  $20–30
First time dining here with a bunch of friends, and let me tell you — the hardest part was deciding what to order. Everything sounded so good that I just trusted my instincts and hoped for the best. Thankfully, the food absolutely delivered.

I went with the Jerusalem Breakfast: herbed scrambled eggs, zaatar labneh, avocado, tomato salad, Syrian olives, and sesame bread. It was light but incredibly satisfying — fresh, flavorful, and perfectly balanced. We also ordered hummus with pita, and it was exactly what hummus should be: smooth, fresh, and dangerously easy to keep dipping into.

The Challah French Toast with mixed berry purée and cinnamon whipped cream? Unreal. Not overly sweet, beautifully balanced, and honestly hard to share. I wish I had photos of everything, but we were too busy enjoying every bite.

We sampled a few desserts, and the knafeh completely stole the show — warm, sweet, and unforgettable. The chocolate mousse was rich and hard to put down, and the malabi was light and refreshing, the perfect way to end the meal.

Overall, we had such a great time. The staff was attentive and welcoming, and the atmosphere felt cozy and homey. If you’re looking for quality Mediterranean food that won’t break the bank, this is definitely a spot worth visiting!!!!
